====================================================================================================
v131  SHOTS TO A TARGET LOSS, not shots to a target cosine
====================================================================================================
  v130 matched the arms at equal per-epoch cos and got a 796-shot
  break-even. Wrong criterion: an optimiser needs to descend, not to
  align. SGD converges at cos ~0.1; SPSA's cos is ~1/sqrt(M) by
  construction and it still works. TIER A, both arms drive their own
  descent, counts from q.ncircuits / q.nshots.

  Exact-gradient descent reaches mean MSE 0.00194 over 3 seeds.
  TARGET = 3x that floor = 0.00583 - a level both arms could reach.

